*Solution Steps Walkthrough:*

1. Recall the definition of a unitary matrix ($U^dagger U = I$) or a Hermitian matrix ($H^dagger = H$).

2. Calculate the conjugate transpose (adjoint) of the matrix by transposing it and taking the complex conjugate of all elements.

3. Perform the matrix multiplication ($U^dagger U$ or check $H^dagger = H$) and equate the result to the identity matrix $I$ (or to the original matrix).

4. Solve the resulting system of algebraic equations for the unknown parameters to satisfy the condition.
